---
const steps = [
  { when: "Before it writes", tools: ["onus_impact", "onus_dependents", "onus_tests_for", "onus_invariants"], body: "What a change would break, who uses it, and which tests cover it." },
  { when: "Before it finishes", tools: ["onus_check"], body: "The changes in meaning of its own work, with a checklist of what to verify." },
  { when: "To hand work in", tools: ["onus_env_run", "onus_submit", "onus_judge"], body: "Tests run in an environment, a submission with that evidence, the judge's verdict." },
  { when: "When it needs more", tools: ["onus_escalate", "onus_escalation"], body: "Rights its token lacks, asked for with evidence and decided by policy or a person." },
];
const agents = ["Claude Code", "Codex", "Copilot", "Cursor", "Devin", "Jules", "Aider"];
---

<section class="chapter" id="agents" data-phase="6" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapter-copy wide">
      <h2 class="display-l" id="agents-title">Any agent. Same rules.</h2>
      <p class="body-l">
        Onus isn't an agent and doesn't pick one for you. Agents work through it over MCP, or a CLI if they can run a
        shell command. Each gets the same scopes, lanes and judge, and earns its own track record.
      </p>
      <pre class="o-code"><code><span class="o-code__line"><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>claude mcp add onus -- onus mcp</span><span class="o-code__line o-code__line--quiet"># any MCP client: onus mcp</span></code></pre>
      <ol class="steps">
        {
          steps.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <h3 class="title">{s.when}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{s.body}</p>
              <p class="tools">
                {s.tools.map((t) => (
                  <code class="code">{t}</code>
                ))}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="body muted">
        Agents cannot approve themselves: they cannot record outcomes, grant escalations, mint tokens or choose the scope
        they are checked against. Pull requests are attributed to {agents.slice(0, -1).join(", ")} and {agents.at(-1)} by
        their branch or bot, and to anything else by an <code class="code">Onus-Agent:</code> trailer.
      </p>
      <p class="display-s swap">Swap every agent overnight and nothing in Onus changes. Only the track records start fresh.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .wide {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .wide .body-l {
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .o-code {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .prompt {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 11.5rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .steps li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .steps .title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .tools {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .tools .code {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .swap {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 28ch;
  }
</style>
